# 🌡️ Smart Temperature Controlled Fan (Arduino)

## 📌 Project Description
This project controls a fan automatically based on temperature using a TMP36 sensor and Arduino.

## 💡 Concept
- Reads temperature from sensor
- Converts analog value to voltage
- Converts voltage to temperature (°C)
- Controls motor speed using PWM

## ⚙️ Components Used
- Arduino UNO
- TMP36 Temperature Sensor
- DC Motor
- Transistor
- Resistor

## 🔌 Working
- Temperature > 30°C → Fan runs at full speed
- Temperature > 25°C → Medium speed
- Temperature < 25°C → Fan OFF

## 🧠 What I Learned
- Sensor Interfacing
- ADC (Analog to Digital Conversion)
- Data Conversion (Voltage → Temperature)
- PWM motor control
- Debugging errors

## 💻 Code
```c
int tempPin = A0;
int motorPin = 9;

void setup() {
  pinMode(motorPin, OUTPUT);
  Serial.begin(9600);
}

void loop() {
  int sensorValue = analogRead(tempPin);
  float voltage = sensorValue * (5.0 / 1023.0);
  float temperature = (voltage - 0.5) * 100;

  if (temperature > 30) {
    analogWrite(motorPin, 255);
  } else if (temperature > 25) {
    analogWrite(motorPin, 150);
  } else {
    analogWrite(motorPin, 0);
  }

  delay(1000);
}
